agm: 1.0
package: auth.platform
version: 0.1.0
title: Authentication Platform Core Rules

node auth.facts.jwt_lifecycle
type: facts
summary: JWT tokens issued by the auth service have a 15-minute expiry with 7-day refresh tokens
priority: critical
stability: high
items:
  - access_token_ttl_15_minutes
  - refresh_token_ttl_7_days
  - refresh_tokens_are_rotating
  - revoked_tokens_checked_against_blocklist
detail:
  Access tokens are short-lived to limit blast radius on compromise.
  Refresh tokens rotate on every use; the previous token is immediately invalidated.
  A token blocklist (Redis, TTL-keyed) stores revoked JTI values.
notes: Tokens are signed with RS256. Public key rotation happens every 90 days.
